WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.020
Revenge of the peppers!

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.440
Enemy carrots!

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.860
Grudge of the eggplants!

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.990
Desire of the cucumbers!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.000
Whoa there! This guy's got a funny look on his face!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.540
Dont'cha think, Droit?

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.420
This is Block D-22.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.970
A disturbance has appeared amidst the Duel Carnival.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.050
Someone making their own special rules.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.390
Take a look at this!

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.270
H-Hey!

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.560
No, this is...

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.440
Tomato juice.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.940
The hell's up with that?!

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.240
I can't work up the strength without my Duel Lunch!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.580
Yuma, you shouldn't eat so fast.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.790
But I'm really hungry here!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.500
Gosh...

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.710
H-Hey!

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.090
Hey, wait up!

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.300
Hold on!

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.470
My Duel Lunch...

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.890
Whatcha lyin' around on the ground like that for?

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.480
Here! Eat my cucumber!

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.060
It'll make you feel good!

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.650
Delicious!

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.190
What the heck is this? It's really yummy!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.240
It really is! It's delicious!

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.740
Did you grow these yourself?

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.620
They taste really good!

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.580
I-I did.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.000
Wow man, they taste so good!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.750
I'm Yuma Tsukumo! Thanks!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.630
What's wrong?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.260
<i>What an angelic smile!</i>

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.300
Huh?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.970
I-I'm Yasai Housaku!

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.270
Out of all vegetables, I like tomatoes the best!

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:13.980
Don't you think it would be great if we turned this city into a tomato paradise?!

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.530
T-Tomato paradise?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.450
Yessir'ee! A tomato-based theme park operated entirely by tomatoes!

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:27.580
If I win the Duel Carnival, I will make this city into a tomato paradise!

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.420
A-And when I do, will you over there with that smile as bright as a tomato...

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.090
W-Will you...?

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.050
Huh?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.670
Will you act as my tomato paradise dream girl?!

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.050
HUH?!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.600
I'm a tomato dream girl...?

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.480
A dream girl...?

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.980
Hi! I'm Tomato-<i>chan</i>!

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.480
I won't let you.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.990
You won't get away with this!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:00.990
Yuma!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.070
Housaku, I won't ever forget about the vegetables you gave me.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.040
But the path we choose to walk is far too different!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.500
Yuma, you...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.750
Face me, Housaku!

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.790
Fascinating!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.710
I will win this Duel Carnival and create my tomato paradise!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.550
And I'll make Kotori-<i>chan</i> into my dream girl!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:28.810
You're full of crap! I swear I'm gonna break your ambitions into pieces!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.310
Yuma...

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.980
Here I come! I'm bringin' it to ya!!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.170
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:42.220
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:49.480
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:58.740
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.240
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.700
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:14.500
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.170
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:25.430
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.310
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.600
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.770
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.360
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.530
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:48.080
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.580
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.580
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:04:53.580 --> 00:05:00.380
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.570
Duel!!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.920
Hey, Yuma... We're gonna be usin' some original rules for this Duel.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.920
"Number 30: Yuma’s Greatest Ordeal! 
Fight to Death: Vegetable Death Match!"

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.880
O-Original rules?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.290
This here!

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.300
Before you can attack, you have to pick out a vegetable from the vegetables in that basket.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.470
You must eat that vegetable before you can attack!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.180
I dun called it the "Vegetable Death Match"!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.690
Wh-What the heck?! As if I'll accept a bunch of rules you just pulled out of thin air!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.400
You guys're sure in high spirits!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.490
Interesting! As the acting referee of the Duel Carnival, I hereby accept those rules!

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:52.830
Hey! Yasai, ya rascal, I guess you were the one stirring up all that commotion throughout the city.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.250
Goshu!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.710
Don't act on your own!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.790
But it's all fine, Droit!

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.880
You're ruining the mood!

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.130
This "Death Match" of Yasai's is pretty amusing!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.840
You betcha!

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.590
H-Hang the heck on!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.390
That gives Yasai Housaku the complete advantage!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.180
What's the big deal, kid?

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.850
You trying to say you don't like Yasai?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.730
You shouldn't be so spiteful.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.060
Th-That's not it!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.860
I'm totally not being spiteful!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.320
Then I take that as an agreement.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.780
I approve Yasai's Death Match.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.280
H-Hey!

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.160
Well then, good luck!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.620
Hey, hold on!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.330
Good deal! That gives me the right to go first!

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.710
My turn! Draw!

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.340
I activate the Field Magic, Tomato Paradise!

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:50.760
With this card, I get to Special Summon one "Tomatoken" when I Summon a Plant-Type Monster!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.180
Tomato Paradise?!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.970
He really made it happen!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:58.140
I Summon Tomatorooper!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.900
Tomatorooper's a Plant-Type.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.530
So I Special Summon a "Tomatoken"!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.910
A tomato Monster!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:15.200
Just how obsessed with tomatoes can a guy be?!

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.910
Then I activate the Continuous Magic, Catapultomato!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:24.590
I release a Plant-Type Monster to inflict 400 points of damage to you!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.340
Eat this red tomato arrow!

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.020
Eatin' a tomato on the edge of death makes for good eatin'!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.100
I dun ended my turn!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:46.770
Dammit! Tomato this, tomato that! I'll beat your deck to a pulp!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.360
You can do it, Yuma!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.400
My turn! Draw!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.450
I Summon Achacha Archer!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:05.420
Achacha Archer inflicts 500 points of damage to the player when it's Summoned.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.550
Go! Achacha Archer!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.800
Good! Then, use Achacha Archer to attack Tomatorooper!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.970
Yup!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.470
In order to attack...

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:25.270
I have to eat one of the vegetables in this basket in order to attack?

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.810
Hurry an' pick one!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.230
I know!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.160
This texture... It's so smooth and long!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.200
It's an... eggplant!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.950
The hell is this?!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.620
That's an eggplant tomato I refurbished from the brink of death!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.710
It's a wonderful tomato you can do almost anything with!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.840
Darn!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:55.340
I set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.930
Yuma, why didn't you attack?

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.470
Are you still feeling your opponent out?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.230
Dueling and vegetables are all about the timing.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.810
You'll come to regret not attacking me!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.900
My turn! Draw!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.650
I Summon Tomatomatryoshka!

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:19.580
When this card is Summoned, I can Special Summon another Tomatomatryoshka from my hand or deck!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.700
Tomatomatryoshka is a Plant-Type!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.630
Thus, Tomato Paradise's effect allows me to Special Summon two "Tomatokens"!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.960
F-Five Tomato Monsters?!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.380
This is my tomato paradise!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:39.970
Then I activate the Continuous Magic, Tomatomatrix!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:46.640
This card increases the Attack Power of all Plant-Type Monsters on my field by 500 points until the End Phase!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.610
The Tomato Magic will power up this huge tomato family even further!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:57.240
And I'll draw a random vegetable from my basket as the rules of this Vegetable Death Match state!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.910
Got a pepper!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.240
Delicious!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.950
Yuma, it's coming!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.960
I use Tomatorooper to attack Achacha Archer!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.960
Tomato Striker!!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.720
Then I direct attack with Tomatomatryoshka!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.140
Go! Hit of the Tomatoes!!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:29.940
How's that?! One more direct attack an' I'll be the winner!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.400
Gosh, get your act together!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.320
Yuma! It's a Trap!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.610
Yup!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.900
I activate the Trap Card, Heartfelt Appeal!

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:49.580
When I take damage during a direct attack, I gain control of the Monster on your field with the highest Defense Power until my next turn.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:53.340
It looks like Tomatomatryoshka has the highest Defense Power.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.380
Great!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:58.510
I'll take the Tomatomatryoshka that hasn't attacked yet!

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.930
Guess that means I can't attack, eh?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.430
But I still got the effect of the Catapultomato Continuous Magic!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:13.360
I'll release two "Tomatokens" for 500 points of damage!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.480
Eat this red tomato arrow!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.110
That ends my turn!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.000
I'm covered in tomato juice!

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.330
Are you okay, Yuma?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.040
Darnit!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.130
My turn, draw!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:39.090
I release Tomatomatryoshka to Advance Summon Chacchaka Archer!

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:48.060
Once per turn, Chacchaka Archer can destroy one Magic or Trap Card on the field.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.390
Oh yeah!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.650
I'll use Chacchaka Archer's effect to destroy Catapultomato!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.740
I'll then activate the Magic Card, Unprecedented Wind!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.660
It increases the Attack Power of a Monster on my field by 1000 points!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.660
Nicely done. Yuma, attack!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.330
A-Attack?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.750
I gotta draw a vegetable to attack!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.420
This feels... tough and bulky!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.090
It's gotta be... a cucumber!

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.430
Yuma, are cucumbers normally red in color?

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.310
Another tomato?!

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.940
That's a cucumber tomato I refurbished from the brink of death!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:39.730
It's really hard! Its crisp texture makes it a topnotch appetizer!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.740
That ain't fair, ya jerk!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:48.200
How's it unfair? I'm just testing possibilities of tomatoes!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.790
Damn you, always going on and on about tomatoes!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:55.870
Yuma...?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.840
This... tomato!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.960
Yuma, what's wrong with you?!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:03.340
If you don't eat it, you'll never get to attack!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.350
No, I can't do it!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:15.350
What?!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.440
Hey, Yuma... Could it be you...?

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:24.360
That's right! I hate tomatoes!

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.240
You hate tomatoes?

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.240
They're evil!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:34.660
Yeah, I don't like tomatoes! No way I can eat 'em!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.960
So that's why you were so desperate to Duel him.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:42.710
Th-Then, you weren't fighting for me...?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.050
Huh? What the heck you talkin' 'bout?

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.510
F-Forget it!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.220
Kotori?!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.180
Next time I'll make you a tomato-flavored Duel Lunch.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:56.600
A-Anyway, I'll set a card face-down and end my turn.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.480
So you hate tomatoes?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.110
You won't eat my tomatoes?!

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.030
S-Say wha?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:11.490
I won't forgive anyone who dares to talk badly of my vegetables!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.660
First I'll make you repent for your hatred of vegetables!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.210
Then I'll create my tomato paradise!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:23.300
Shut up! I could care less if you create a tomato paradise!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:28.760
You bastard! I swear to win this in order to realize my dream!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.010
My turn! Draw!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.810
I Summon Tomatomatryoshka!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.600
Then I Special Summon a "Tomatoken"!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.190
What?!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.400
He's got three Level Three Monsters.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.320
I Overlay my two "Tomatokens" and my Tomatomatryoshka!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.320
I build the Overlay Network with these three Monsters!

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.240
Xyz Summon!

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.830
Appear before us! Bless the Earth! Swallow the sun!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:00.040
Tomato Monarch: Dread King!

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:06.760
C-Cute!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:11.140
I use Tomato Paradise's effect to Special Summon a "Tomatoken"!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.720
I then activate Tomato Monarch: Dread King's effect!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:24.690
Once per turn, I can detach one of its Overlay Units to double its original Attack Power until the Standby Phase of my next turn!

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:32.820
This time it's a tomato goblin?! And its Attack Power's 3200!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:38.040
This is it! Dread King, attack Chacchaka Archer!

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.620
Roasted Tomato Splasher!!

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.300
Yuma!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.930
Good deal! It's my vict-

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.680
Why do ya still got Life?!

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.810
'Coz I activated Summon Transaction!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:09.440
This card activated if I have a Monster with 1000 or less Attack Power in my hand when a Monster I control is attacked.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:17.910
The battle damage is reduced by 500 points and I Special Summon a Monster from my hand with 1000 or less Attack Points!

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.370
Come out, Gagaga Girl!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:27.170
In exchange, my opponent's Monster can't be destroyed in battle by the Monster Special Summoned

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:30.880
by Summon Transaction's effect for two turns.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.220
Fine then. You only got 400 Life Points left.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.810
There's no way a guy who hates tomatoes is gonna beat me!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.100
Turn end.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.850
My turn! Draw!

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.730
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.280
Yuma, change Gagaga Magician's level.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:51.780
Right!

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.160
I change Gagaga Magician's level from four to three!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.570
Yuma, the rest is up to you.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:03.000
If you Xyz Summon, our setup for victory will be in place.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.750
But you will have to eat a vegetable in order to allow that to happen.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:11.710
R-Right, I'll have to eat one of the vegetables in this basket...

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.010
This time I'll grab anything other than a tomato!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.390
This... This feeling in my hand...

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.350
There's no way it's a tomato!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.440
It's a carrot!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.610
That's a crossbred carrot and tomato I grew called a carrato.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.650
Damn it!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:39.530
Come on, Yuma! Eat that tomato!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.790
She's right, Yuma! If you keep this up, you'll lose!

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.080
Can it!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.080
Say what you want, but there's no way I'm gonna eat a tomato!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:53.380
And you're fine with losing and allowing Housaku-<i>kun</i> to win and create his tomato paradise?!

00:17:54.720 --> 00:18:05.270
If that happens, I'll go to your house and make you eat tomato salad, tomato pizza, and tomato Duel Lunches every single day!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.730
What!?

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:11.190
If you don't want that, you better eat that <i>whole</i> tomato right now!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.770
B-But...

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.070
She's right, Yuma!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:17.200
You have no other choice if you want to beat him!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.160
Now! Eat it!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.370
Yuma!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:27.120
Shut up! I know! I just have to eat this darn thing, right?!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.050
I'm gonna bring it to me!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.550
Huh? That's really good!

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.550
Yuma!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.520
I've never eaten anything so good!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.640
Glad to hear, Yuma! You ate it!

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.480
You finally ate it!

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:54.650
Now you can beat him, Yuma! Xyz Summon!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.190
Right!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:19:00.160
I Overlay my Level Three Gagaga Girl and Gagaga Magician!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.950
I build the Overlay Network with these two Monsters!

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.750
Xyz Summon!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.250
Come on out, my new friend!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.630
Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:20.630
And when Gagaga Girl is used as Xyz Material with another Gagaga Monster,

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:24.930
she can reduce the Attack Power of one of the opponent's Xyz Monsters to zero!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.720
Zero-Zero Call!

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.360
My Dread King!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:40.320
Go, Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.860
Attack Tomato Monarch: Dread King!

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.280
Melody Wave!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:52.920
And now, Dread King won't be destroyed because of Summon Transaction's effect!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.420
But you'll still take the damage!

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.050
And now for Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody's Xyz Effect!

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:08.310
Right! Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody can detach one of her Overlay Units

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:13.270
to attack once again if there's an Xyz Monster on the opponent's side of the field!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.070
Housaku, your tomatoes are the best!

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:25.120
Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody, attack Tomato Monarch: Dread King!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:31.500
I'll activate Brass Fiend Mero Mero Melody's Xyz Effect once again!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.920
Go, Mero Mero Melody!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.630
Melody Wave!!

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:48.430
My tomatoes! I'm shining just like my tomatoes!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.560
Heck yeah!

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.110
Hey! You okay, Housaku?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.530
Hey!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.030
Yuma!

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.290
Sorry about that. I realized thanks to you.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.540
Tomatoes are really delicious!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:22.340
I won the Duel, but your strong feelings towards tomatoes were stronger than mine.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.970
Whaccha talkin' about?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:28.550
I lost the Duel because of your strong desire to like tomatoes!

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:33.600
I got to see a lonely man ascend to the land of tomatoes!

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:35.100
I was deeply moved!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.060
Housaku!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:39.020
Yuma, my dear tomato friend!

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:48.870
See ya later.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:56.500
He's a bit of an oddball, but he's a good guy!

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.250
You're right.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.210
Observation #16...

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.880
"Bring it to 'em" means "loving tomatoes".

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:09.800
Oh yeah! I'm gonna keep this up and win the entire tournament!

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:23.110
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:29.030
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:34.950
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:38.000
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.590
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:45.670
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.470
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:52.930
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.970
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:59.270
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:06.360
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:09.400
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:13.870
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:15.830
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:17.620
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:23.000
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:26.050
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:29.630
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:34.050
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:35.890
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.180
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:44.860
My sister suddenly ordered me to capture some man!

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:48.230
But the guy has created one miracle after another!

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:52.410
Awesome! So only the luckiest people can use that card?

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.780
So he really has Number 7!

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.490
My Numbers!

00:23:57.490 --> 00:24:01.540
If his powers are real, then this Duel...

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:03.540
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:07.090
"His name is Charlie, the Man with Strongest Luck in History"

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.210
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!
